daa29a26 (2663 1793852217668 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f426") (src . "scope: reduce the store once at a literal cut, not once per root\n\nscope --roots all read every root with its own read at the cut, and\neach such read reduced the whole store again: 612 roots at 5.4 s each,\n99 percent of a 56 minute scope, the per-root cost flat whatever the\nroot's size. Now, where a routed read would be answered in this process\n(THEOURGIA_LOCAL=1, or no socket at the store's path), scope obtains\nthe state at a literal cut once, with the function a read at a cut\nobtains it with (the cut judged usable, one restricted replay, the\nserved cut asked again), and reads every root from that state through\nthe read handler. A tag cut, a refusal of that function, or a daemon\nserving the store keep the routed read per root, so the answer is the\nstore's own on every path and a serving daemon still reads the blocks\nit scopes.\n\nThe restricted replay of a read at a cut is a seam phase of its own,\ncut-replay, bare without THEOURGIA_TIMING, so a test can count the\nreductions a verb makes. local-route? is routed's test in one place.\n\nTests: test/scope-once.sc (new, 6 rows: one cut-replay line per scope\nat a literal cut and one per root at a tag or with a socket present;\nevery root's state read equal to its routed read; the copies and the\nmissing-writer refusals unchanged); rows-baseline gains its row.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 625))))
